What this is for
----------------
An internal working asset. It exists so that an AI assistant can be given a
clean, searchable copy of the product documentation and answer from it, and so
that demonstrations of that idea can be built and shown. It is a mirror, so it
lags upstream, and the upstream sites remain the authority. Check the dates in
README.md before relying on any page.

Where the material came from
----------------------------
Most of it comes from public sites: the devnet and Composer Help Centres, the
Mintlify SI docs, and OpenAPI documents served by Composer and Logi Report
instances. Two exceptions are worth naming rather than leaving to be
discovered. simba-intelligence/reverse-engineered/ was captured against running
SI instances where the published docs are silent or lag the release, including
the product's own generated API specification. One file in that folder,
26.2-release-notes-official.md, states that it was mirrored from an internal
Confluence page.

